<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title><%= @entry.name %> — watch only</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no">
    <%# Nothing here is worth a second look, and a cached copy of a diagnostic is a
        diagnostic of the wrong moment. %>
    <meta http-equiv="Cache-Control" content="no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate">

    <%# No importmap, and no application stylesheet. That omission is the whole layout.
        #watch_only exists to be the control against the watch page, and it can only be one
        if the page really is empty: loading the app's JavaScript would bring Turbo, Stimulus
        and every controller on the pins back onto a page whose point is that none of them
        are here. So the diagnostic script is inline, the handful of rules it needs are
        inline, and what is left between the browser and the provider is one iframe.

        Which also means this page cannot drift as the app changes -- no controller can be
        added to it by accident, because there is nowhere for one to be added. %>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: dark; }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; color: #eee;
                   font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
      /* The stack, copied from the watch page so the rig is a fair reproduction of it: a
         spare is stacked *behind* the live frame rather than hidden, because a frame the
         browser believes nobody can see is one it feels free to stop buffering -- which
         would make the second stream cheaper here than it is there, and prove nothing. */
      .frames { position: relative; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
      .frame { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; }
      .frame--live { z-index: 1; }

      /* Out of the way while a film runs, and legible the moment it is looked at. */
      .hud { position: fixed; top: 0; left: 0; z-index: 10; max-width: min(34rem, 96vw);
             font: 12px/1.45 ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
             background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .72); border-bottom-right-radius: .5rem;
             opacity: .28; transition: opacity .15s; }
      .hud[data-open="true"], .hud:hover, .hud:focus-within { opacity: 1; }
      /* Raised for something that can end a film, and never cleared: an alarm at minute
         three is still the reason the film died at minute forty. */
      .hud[data-alarm="true"] { opacity: 1; background: rgba(90, 0, 0, .85); }
      .hud__bar { display: flex; gap: .75rem; align-items: baseline;
                  padding: .35rem .6rem; cursor: pointer; }
      .hud__title { font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .04em; }
      .hud__count { color: #ffd479; }
      .hud__body { padding: 0 .6rem .5rem; }
      .hud[data-open="false"] .hud__body { display: none; }
      .hud dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 6.5rem 1fr; gap: .1rem .6rem; margin: .3rem 0; }
      .hud dt { color: #8d949e; }
      .hud dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      .hud__log { margin: .4rem 0 .5rem; max-height: 14rem; overflow: auto;
                  border-top: 1px solid #333; padding-top: .35rem; }
      /* Wrapped rather than scrolled sideways: the detail on a line is the reason the
         line is there, and a log you have to drag to read is a log nobody reads. */
      .hud__line { margin-bottom: .15rem; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
      .hud__at { color: #8d949e; }
      .hud__event--reload { color: #ff8a80; font-weight: 700; }
      .hud button, .hud select { font: inherit; color: inherit; background: #222;
                    border: 1px solid #444; border-radius: .25rem; padding: .15rem .5rem;
                    cursor: pointer; max-width: 100%; }
      .hud__tools { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .3rem; align-items: center; }

      /* The rig. Kept visually apart from the readout above it, because everything here
         changes the experiment rather than reporting on it. */
      .hud__rig { margin: .5rem 0; padding: .45rem .5rem; border: 1px solid #4a3d00;
                  border-radius: .3rem; background: rgba(60, 50, 0, .35); }
      .hud__rig h2 { margin: 0 0 .35rem; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .04em;
                     color: #ffd479; }
      .hud__rig label { display: inline-flex; gap: .3rem; align-items: center; }
      .hud__note { margin: .35rem 0 0; color: #8d949e; }

      /* Something is running that would not be running on its own. */
      .hud:not([data-spares="0"]) .hud__rig { border-color: #a05; background: rgba(90, 0, 30, .45); }

      .missing { display: grid; place-content: center; gap: .5rem; height: 100%;
                 padding: 2rem; text-align: center; }
      .missing code { color: #ffd479; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body><%= yield %></body>
</html>
